* 17 Nov 26 Windows port - THREE ANSWERS, as its callers already read it: a group Windows says does not exist is @false with status
*           0, and only a lookup that could not be made is status 1.  Both were status 1, so create_account check.files.group, modifya
*           (files, ai, route and key groups) and set.ai reported a missing group as 10081 "unable to change ... status 1" where they
*           meant 10024 "not a valid Windows group" (found by the audit's second pass).  The caller's fail-closed result is unchanged:
*           @false either way.
* 14 Aug 26 Windows port - ask Windows instead of reading /etc/group, which
*           does not exist on the MSYS2 runtime.  See the description.
* rev 0.9.0 Jan 25 mab initial commit
* END-HISTORY
*
* START-DESCRIPTION:
*
*    x = !is_group(group)
*
*    Is group a Windows local group?
*
*    This function sets the STATUS() value to 0 if successful, 1 if the
*    specified group does not exist.
*
*    WHY THIS NO LONGER READS /etc/group - the same defect !is_grp_member and
*    !is_user had, and the third of the three: MSYS2 dropped /etc/group, the
*    read failed, and this answered false for every group.  Measured
*    14 Aug 2026: no /etc/group under either root the runtime can use, while
*    Get-LocalGroup returned sdu_sdacct5 with its SID from the same machine.
*
*    WHAT IT BROKE: DELACC gates the removal of an account's sdu_ group on
*    this (line 191), so DELETE.ACCOUNT silently skipped it and left the group
*    behind on every account it ever removed.  CREATEA's create.group asks it
*    too.
*
*    LOCAL GROUPS ONLY, matching !is_grp_member and !os_group.
*
* END-DESCRIPTION
*
* START-CODE

$internal
function is_group(group)
$catalog !is_group

deffun valid_os_name(name) calling '!valid_os_name'

group_found = @false
set.status 0
* Modified by Composer AI - 2026/06/10.
* Empty group name cannot match; avoid a pointless lookup.
if group = '' then
   set.status 1
   return group_found
end
* --------------------

* 14 Aug 26 Windows port - validated before being interpolated into the
*   command below, as in !is_grp_member.
if not(valid_os_name(group)) then
   set.status 1
   return group_found
end

* 14 Aug 26 Windows port - SH1 names PowerShell, so the command IS the script.
*  17 Nov 26: exit 0 found, 3 Windows says there is no such group (GroupNotFoundException), anything else could not tell.
*  3 rather than 1 so that PowerShell failing to start or to parse (which exits 1) is never read as "no such group".
   ps = 'try { if (Get-LocalGroup -Name "' : group
   ps := '" -ErrorAction Stop) { exit 0 } } catch [Microsoft.PowerShell.Commands.GroupNotFoundException] { exit 3 } catch { exit 2 }; exit 2'

   os.execute ps

   gf.rc = os.error()
   begin case
      case gf.rc = 0
         group_found = @true
      case gf.rc = 3
         null      ;* no such group: @false, status 0
      case 1
         * PowerShell could not be run, or the lookup failed: the caller cannot confirm the group and must not act on it.
         set.status 1
   end case

return group_found
end
